James sought advice on how to format a numerical range in LaTeX that spans zero, specifically the expression `-2.8--+11.9%`, noting the disparity in size between the negative and positive signs. I clarified that since it was in regular text, formatting options would differ from math mode. I proposed formatting solutions, including using `\text{}` for uniformity and explicit spacing with `\,`, ultimately suggesting bold formatting with `\textbf{}` for a balanced appearance.
